What does the following snippet print when evaluating method calls across multiple inheritance levels?

```java
class BaseWorker {
    int compute(int x) {
        return x + 1;
    }
}
class IntermediateWorker extends BaseWorker {
    int compute(int x) {
        return super.compute(x) * 2;
    }
}
class FinalWorker extends IntermediateWorker {
    int compute(int x) {
        return super.compute(x) + 5;
    }
}
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        FinalWorker worker = new FinalWorker();
        System.out.println(worker.compute(3));
    }
}
```

Trace object identity when super is compared to this. What does the following program print?

```java
class SuperIdentity {
    boolean checkSelf(Object other) {
        return this == other;
    }
}
class SubIdentity extends SuperIdentity {
    void test() {
        System.out.println(super.checkSelf(this));
    }
}
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        new SubIdentity().test();
    }
}
```
